To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: Restricting memory used by OSF/1
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96075318306709


 The procedure used to restrict memory used by OSF/1 to some 
 number <= the actual physical memory installed is;
 
 1) perform an interactive boot
    >>> boot -fl i
 
 2) When the option prompt appears, type
        vmunix memlimit=XXX
  
  Where XXX is the amount of memory (in megabytes) you want 
 available. This value persists across reboots apparently, so 
 it has to be reset manually to the full amount once the experiment
 has finished.
  
