My original questions and very abbreviated answers:

>Can anyone tell me what is involved in switching from OSF/1 v2.1 
>sendmail to Sendmail.8.6.10?  Am I going to have to put a lot of work 
>into redoing the configuration files?

No. Sendmail v8 use a lot of m4 files to define most of the features used
in standart config. You just have to write a .mc file (actually in m4) 
which describe which feature you want to use. Have a look in the sendmail 
op guide and in the README file in the sendmail/cf directory, almost 
everything is explained.

Well, last comment is true if you *DO NOT* run decnet. Sendmail v8 m4 
config does *NOT* include decnet support. If you use decnet, you will either 
have to tweak the .cf file (not recommended since .cf are automatically 
rebuild when you modify the .mc file or upgrade) or tweak the .mc file 
(local mods to rulesets). Maybe you will need to do some more work (rewrite 
.cf file ?)

>How about installing the daemon(s)?  Do I need to schedule a reboot or 
>can I simply kill the running process and start up the other?

do a 'make install-sendmail' and then 'sh /sbin/init.d/sendmail restart'

>Are there any known bugs with v8.6.10 for OSF/1 that should make me 
>reconsider the update?

Use 8.6.11

First off, you should run 8.6.11 rather than 8.6.10 because it does
fix a problem with running the Berkeley DB code on Alphas.  The
Berkeley DB code can be used for alias tables and various other
tables that sendmail can make use of.

There are no known bugs in v8.6.11 - yet.

Improvements include better IDENT handling, 64 bit fixes for makemap
and less paranoia when handling messages from Pine.

