Hi,

I was trying to set up a modem on DEC Alpha 3000/300 OSF/1 3.0B, using 
the methods discussed in this list.  When dialing from a PC, it gets 
connected but nothing else happens, no login prompt or anything.  What
am I missing?  Here's what I did:

   . Edit /etc/gettydefs to include line

       dialin# B38400 HUPCL CS8 # B38400 HUPCL CS8 #login: #dialin

   . Edit /etc/inittab to include line

       dialin:23:respawn:/usr/sbin/getty -h /dev/tty00 dialin vt100

   . Set the modem (Hayes, V.32bis) on a PC and save the settings:

       Auto Answer, Hardware Flow Control, 14,400-8-N-1, 
       MNP5 and V.42bis compression, Auto-reliable

   . Run 'init q' to restart init

   . Dial from a PC.  It says 'connected'.  The RD flashes for a while 
     and then goes out.  No login prompt is displayed.


