Subject: Summary: enabling more users on OSF/1
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96075318306434


I had said that I had problems getting more than 2-3 users running on
our OSF/1 systems. A few people pointed out that I need the OSF-USR
PAK to do this, but it was loaded..

From: luchini@siberia.ups-tlse.fr (Marco Luchini)

mentioned..

>Don't you need the OSF-USR license as well?  I found that under 3.0
>OSF-BASE created its own restricted OSF-USR license.  Using lmf issue to
>get rid of it followed by lmf reset enables the OSF-USR that you
>actually want, to run.  None of this was necessary under OSF2.0.

I found the license OSF-BASE-IMPLICIT-USER to be loaded, so I did the
following on all of our machines:

	lmf delete OSF-USR DEC OSF-BASE-IMPLICIT-USER
	lmf load 100 OSF-USR
	lmf reset

and this appears to work.

