It turned out that the software packages from DIGITAL, at least here,
in Germany are different from those in USA and we got the updates within
our Software Contract with a delay of 3 month.
P01 here has the Part number AV-PROPP-TE, from DEC 94, 
but is labeled with Nov 94.
P01 on other sides has the part number QA-054AA-H8 P01.
The Labels here in Germany and in USA are different.
Mail me, if you want more Details.

So far so ...


But the basic Problem I have is :

I had to install PATHWORKS for OSF/1 v3.0
We need 
	a. File Services
	b. Print Services
	c. REMOTEBOOT

We have :
	a. several Pc's with DEPCA Ethernet Controller
	b. A VAX (!!) with is able to serve remote boot request.
	   You can't serve remote boot with ULTRIX, not when you have DEPCA.

	c. An Alpha 3000/600 with OSF/1 v3.0 which should now be
	   the Pathworks server.


1. I first installed Pathworks  - nothing happened.
2. I installed NETbeui      - nothing happened.
   Then someone told me to install DECnet (!!) for remote boot, even if
   I never use DECnet. I waited for DECnet OSI 3.0.
   I figured out, that 
	a. the DEPCA Controller are requesting the boot services with mop.
	b. the mop boot server for OSF/1 v3.0 is on the DECnet OSI 3.0
	   Software Package.
	c. I have to install DECnet OSI

2. I installed DECnet OSI       - nothing happened. 
3. I made a FRB (Floppy Remote Boot) Floppy Disk for one PC.
4. I tried to boot remote and observed the network with an analyser.

I turned out that

The DEPCA is sending 
1. C   64 PC       -> DECmop RemCo DEC MOP Rem Con
2. C   64 PC       -> DECmop DuLoa DEC MOP Dump/Load

